Modifications applied by subAnimJ
---------------------------------

For each kanji listed in `targets/`, the corresponding SVG file under
`svgsJa/` and the entry in `graphicsJa.txt` are modified relative to the
upstream animCJK release. Modifications include:

1. Stroke extension: certain strokes that, by font design, do not connect
   to neighboring strokes are extended along their tangent until they meet
   another stroke. Examples: middle horizontal of "日" (3rd stroke),
   middle horizontal of "田" (4th stroke).

2. Radical replacement (compose): the Chinese-style "thread" (糸偏),
   "bamboo" (竹冠), and "woman" (女偏) radicals in selected kanji are
   replaced with hand-authored Japanese-style equivalents stored under
   `parts/`. The hand-authored radical SVGs are MIT licensed; the resulting
   composed kanji SVGs remain under the APL.

3. Punctuation generation (Klee-derived): the eight Japanese punctuation
   marks listed above are generated by `tools/extract_punct.py` from Klee
   One outlines plus hand-defined median paths.

The exact list of changes per kanji is recorded in `targets/{kanji}.jsonl`.

Each modified file therefore differs from the upstream copy. The upstream
copies are preserved unchanged inside the `vendor/animCJK` and `vendor/Klee`
git submodules for reference and to allow regeneration via `make build`.
